# vTual — identity, claims, management

- **User ≠ vTuber Profile.** `users` is the login; `vtual_creators` is the public profile. Membership is **private**: never expose that two profiles share one User, never add a user-listing endpoint.
- **Creator access:** `vtual_creator_members` (`owner`|`editor`|`viewer`) or staff `manage any vtual resource`. `CreatorAccessService::memberRoleFor` ignores the staff override; `roleFor` still reports staff as Owner for legacy callers. A management member with an active assignment gets authority through `managementRoleForCreator` (org Owner/Admin → view + mutate, org Staff → view only).
- **Claims:** claim an **orphan** (no `owner` member). Bio token is bound to the proof channel; Discord path binds private discovered channels (`verified_via=discord_connection`, promote to public). On success: `owner` member + product role `Vtual vTuber`, all competing pendings close `cancelled` + `closed_reason=superseded`. Rows are kept as audit — never hard-delete.
- **Claim guards:** check claimable **before** burning an attempt; creator row lock + `closeCompetingClaims` on the winner path (no silent steal); caps `max_pending_per_user`, cooldown, max attempts → `max_attempts` close + 24 h block per creator; restarting cancels the prior pending (`user_cancel`) without double-counting.
- **One proof channel owns the whole profile** — never claim every listed channel. `verified_channel_id` is the contract channel, `channel_id` the bio proof.
- **Staff Accept Anyway** is synchronous and gated by `vtual.claim.accept_anyway_enabled` (Tier B).
- **Managements** (`vtual_managements`) are talent orgs, unrelated to the core Spatie role `Management`. Archiving requires a real Owner/Admin **membership** row — `manage any vtual resource` alone never grants archive power (no superuser bypass).
- **Onboarding is invite-only** (privacy): no user-listing endpoint, email-based, unknown email 404 `invite_user_not_found`, self-invite/existing-member/duplicate-pending 422. **Member removal is the invite endpoint** — `DELETE /managements/{id}/invites/{inviteId}` on an accepted invite removes the membership and marks it `revoked` in one transaction; no `DELETE /members/{memberId}` exists. Roles assignable via API are `admin`/`staff` only (owner comes from org create), no self-edit, last-owner guard 422 `last_owner`. Tokens never appear in API listings.
- **Management claim (orphan → Owner):** staff create owner-less orgs (`POST /managements/orphan`); handover is an Owner-role invite allowed only while claimable.
- **Creator invites** (`mode=existing|new`, `existing` pins a `creator_id` owned by the invitee, verified at send **and** accept) end in an ACTIVE `vtual_management_creators` assignment. Accepting a `new` invite mints an orphan profile + Owner membership + `Vtual vTuber` + implicit activation.
- **Events:** org Owner/Admin create/update/cancel (`assertCanAssignCreators`, staff bypass), publish direct — no moderation. Ended/cancelled are immutable (422 `event_not_actionable`).
- **Merge (absorb):** dual ownership or staff; moves channels/links/contents/appearances/assignments, cancels pending claims `closed_reason=merged`, keeps destination meta, 422 on `(platform_id, external_id)` clash, source archived + members stripped + slug mangled so it is **not claimable**. One-way; no undo.
- **Authorization stack:** `auth:api → product.active:Vtual → permission:<perm> → Policy → service checks`. Product perms `view/create/edit/delete vtual creator|management`, `view/create vtual channel`, `claim vtual creator`, plus staff `view any` / `manage any vtual resource`. Platform credentials and the incident queue use **core** perms `view|manage vtual platform credentials` and `view|manage vtual incident` (Root/Admin); `PlatformCredentialPolicy` re-checks the credential pair.
- **Activation:** `config/products.php` `menu_routes` is the gate (orphans, claims, platform-credentials, profiles). `vtual.managements.index` / `vtual.events.index` are deliberately absent — member-only via `MANAGEMENT_MEMBER_ROUTES` (navigation rule 6).
- **Audit trail:** Spatie `LogsActivity`, log name **`vtual`**, `logFillable` + `logOnlyDirty` + `dontLogEmptyChanges` on Management, ManagementMember, ManagementCreator, ManagementInvite, CreatorManagementInvite, VtualEvent. Invite models `logExcept(['token'])`. Creator/Channel/Content/credentials are deliberately excluded — do not widen `vtual`; give a creator trail its own log name.
- **Realtime:** `vtual.claim.{claimId}` owner-only (`.claim.progress`, payload includes the bio token — safe only because it is owner-only), `vtual.claims` staff ping (`.claim.changed`, ids + action + status **only**), `vtual.creator.{creatorId}` (`.channel.snapshot.updated`), `vtual.management.{managementId}` (`.management.updated`, `kind` = `management|member|invite|creator|creator_invite|creator_grant|event` — all seven, a kind the SPA cannot name is a silently ignored push), `vtual.platform-credentials` (`.platform.credential.changed`), `vtual.incidents` staff-only on `view vtual incident` (`.incident.changed`, ids + enums **only** — incident title/detail are platform free text and never travel). **Never widen a secret-bearing channel — add a sibling and refetch.** There is no "all managements" channel: a cross-management list (`VtualEventsView`) binds one `vtual.management.{id}` channel per org on the page via `syncVtualManagementChannels`. An edit form must not let a push overwrite fields the actor is typing, and must lock itself read-only when the refetched row left an editable status.
- **Membership changes refresh navigation:** `acceptInvite` / `cancelInvite` call `MenuRepository::forgetPresentedTreeForUserId()` + targeted `MenuTreeChanged` (`target_user_id`), so a revoked member's vTual menu entries disappear live.
- **No third-party embeds on guest surfaces:** the public profile **links out** (`url` + `platform_key` on every content item) — no player/chat iframe, and `frame-src` keeps hCaptcha as its only value on both the backend CSP and the SPA `_headers`. Decided and final: [reference-embed-policy.md](../../docs/domains/vtual/reference-embed-policy.md).
- **Seed order is mandatory:** `RoleSeeder` → `ArchivdRoleSeeder` → `VtualRoleSeeder` → `MenuSeeder`; `MenuSeeder` before the role seeders throws naming the missing roles.

